pcap-doctor
===========

Third-party material bundled or fetched by this project:

* `src/pcap_doctor/data/cipher_names.tsv` and `data/cipher_suites.json`
  Cipher-suite names and ids are derived from Wireshark's value table
  (`tshark -G values`). Wireshark is distributed under the GPL-2.0-or-later;
  the extracted *name/id table* is a factual list of IANA-assigned numbers and
  names, redistributed here under the terms in LICENSE.

* `captures/*`
  Sample packet captures from the Wireshark project test suite, fetched by
  `scripts/fetch_captures.sh`, distributed under the BSD 2-Clause License.
  See LICENSE.

* Standard references cited in findings
  RFC 8996, RFC 8999, RFC 7457, RFC 7465, RFC 6194, RFC 5280, RFC 5246,
  RFC 8446, RFC 4568, RFC 3711, RFC 3261, RFC 5764, RFC 7858, RFC 8484,
  RFC 9000, RFC 9001, RFC 9147, and CWE entries. These are cited, not copied.

* `tls.handshake.ja3` / `ja3s`
  Implemented by Wireshark; the fingerprints themselves are computed values,
  not copied data.
